Package: multimod
Title: Define and Render Mathematical Models Across Optimization Languages
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
  c(person(given = "Oleg", 
          family = "Lugovoy", 
          email = "olugovoy@optimalsolution.dev", 
          role = c("aut", "cre"), 
          comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5546-9875")))
Description: A domain-specific language for defining sets, parameters,
    variables, mappings and equations of an algebraic optimization model in R,
    and rendering the model to several mathematical programming languages,
    including 'GAMS', 'GNU MathProg', 'Pyomo' and 'JuMP', or to an LP matrix
    solved in R. Models can be folded, trimmed, validated, compared and
    stored, and solutions read back into R. Linear programs with continuous
    variables are the tested class; integer and binary variables are carried in
    the model and written by some backends, and nonlinear expressions have no
    tested route to a solver.
URL: https://optimal2050.github.io/multimod/, https://github.com/optimal2050/multimod
